<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="u4c-ct-labeled">
  <title>Unit 4c Subgoal Labeled Puzzles for Toggle Code</title>
  <p>
    These are copies of the 2D Arrays Mixed Up Code Practice puzzles with
    subgoal labels added. The 2D Arrays Toggle Code Practice page uses them as
    the Get Help puzzles for its write code problems. Each loop header and its
    opening brace are one block, so one label sits on each loop, and each if
    statement is one block with its body.
  </p>

  <activity label="array2Dex1muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex1muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="show" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment should create a 10 by 10 two-dimensional
        int array. It should fill this array with numbers 0 to 99 from left to
        right, top row to bottom row and print the output (in row-column order).
        But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not
        needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and
        put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button to
        check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>// Create the array with 10 rows and 10 columns</cline>
          <cline>int[][] table = new int[10][10];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>// Create the array with 10 rows and 10 columns</cline>
          <cline>int[][] table = int[10][10];</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>// Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
          <cline>for (int row = 0; row &lt; table.length; row++)</cline>
          <cline>{</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>// Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
          <cline>for (int row = 0; row &lt; table.length(); row++)</cline>
          <cline>{</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>    for (int col = 0; col &lt; table[row].length; col++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>    for (int col = row; col &lt; table[row].length; col++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>        // Set the element at this row and column to its place in reading order</cline>
        <cline>        table[row][col] = col + 10 * row;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>        // Print the element without moving to a new line</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.print(table[row][col] + "\t");</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end inner for loop</cline>
        <cline>} // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex2muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex2muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="show" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment should create a 8 by 8 two-dimensional int
        array. It should fill this array with a checkered pattern of 0s and 1s –
        starting with a 1 in the top left corner and print the output (in
        row-column order). But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra
        blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed
        blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the right.
        Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="5">
        <cline>// Create the array with 8 rows and 8 columns</cline>
        <cline>int[][] checkerboard = new int[8][8];</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>// Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
        <cline>for (int row = 0; row &lt; checkerboard.length; row++)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
        <cline>    for (int col = 0; col &lt; checkerboard[row].length; col++)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Check for a square whose row and column call for 1 and set it</cline>
          <cline>        if ((row + col) % 2 == 0)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            checkerboard[row][col] = 1;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Check for a square whose row and column call for 1 and set it</cline>
          <cline>        if ((row + col) % 2 == 1)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            checkerboard[row][col] = 1;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Check for a square whose row and column call for 1 and set it</cline>
          <cline>        if (row % 2 == 0)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            checkerboard[row][col] = 1;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>        // Print the element without moving to a new line</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.print(checkerboard[row][col] + " ");</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    } // end inner for loop</cline>
        <cline>} // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex3muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex3muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="show" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional int array and return the sum of all of its values. But,
        the blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not
        needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and
        put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button to
        check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="5">
        <cline>public static int sumVals(int[][] nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    // Start the running total at zero</cline>
        <cline>    int sum = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
          <cline>    for (int row = 0; row &lt; nums.length; row++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
          <cline>    for (int row = 0; row &lt;= nums.length; row++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
          <cline>    for (int row = 0; row &lt; nums.length(); row++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int col = 0; col &lt; nums[row].length; col++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int col = 0; col &lt; nums.length; col++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>            // Add the element at this row and column to the running total</cline>
        <cline>            sum += nums[row][col];</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>        } // end inner for loop</cline>
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>    // Return the sum of all the values after checking every element</cline>
        <cline>    return sum;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>} // end sumVals method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex4muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex4muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="show" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional String array “image” and reverse each row from left to
        right. For example: 1 2 3 4 -&gt; 4 3 2 1. But, the blocks have
        been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not needed in a
        correct solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and put them in
        the correct order on the right. Click the Check button to check your
        solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="1">
        <cline>public static void flipImage(String[][] image)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
        <cline>    for (int row = 0; row &lt; image.length; row++)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index in the left half</cline>
        <cline>        for (int col = 0; col &lt; image[0].length / 2; col++)</cline>
        <cline>        {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Swap the element with the one equally far from the row's other end</cline>
          <cline>            String temp = image[row][col];</cline>
          <cline>            image[row][col] = image[row][image[row].length - 1 - col];</cline>
          <cline>            image[row][image[row].length - 1 - col] = temp;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Swap the element with the one equally far from the row's other end</cline>
          <cline>            image[row][col] = image[row][image[row].length - 1 - col];</cline>
          <cline>            image[row][image[row].length - 1 - col] = image[row][col];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Swap the element with the one equally far from the row's other end</cline>
          <cline>            String temp = image[row][col];</cline>
          <cline>            image[row][col] = image[row][image[row].length - col];</cline>
          <cline>            image[row][image[row].length - col] = temp;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>        } // end inner for loop</cline>
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
        <cline>} // end flipImage method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex5muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex5muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional array of ints and edit it such that all even numbers are
        replaced by zero. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra
        blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed
        blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the right.
        Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="2">
        <cline>public static void makeEvenNumsZero(int[][] nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
          <cline>    for (int row = 0; row &lt; nums.length; row++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
          <cline>    for (int row = 0; row &lt; nums[0].length; row++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int col = 0; col &lt; nums[row].length; col++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int col = 0; col &lt; nums[row].length(); col++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Check for an even number and replace it with zero</cline>
          <cline>            if (nums[row][col] % 2 == 0)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                nums[row][col] = 0;</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Check for an even number and replace it with zero</cline>
          <cline>            if (nums[row][col] / 2 == 0)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                nums[row][col] = 0;</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Check for an even number and replace it with zero</cline>
          <cline>            if (nums[row][col] % 2 == 1)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                nums[row][col] = 0;</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>        } // end inner for loop</cline>
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
        <cline>} // end makeEvenNumsZero method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex6muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex6muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional array of ints and a desired int and return the number of
        occurrences of the desired int in the two-dimensional array. But, the
        blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not
        needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and
        put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button to
        check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="2">
        <cline>public static int numOccurrences(int[][] nums, int desired)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    // Start the count of occurrences at zero</cline>
        <cline>    int occurrences = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the array</cline>
        <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; nums.length; i++)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int j = 0; j &lt; nums[i].length; j++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int j = 0; j &lt;= nums[i].length; j++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Check for the desired number and count it</cline>
          <cline>            if (nums[i][j] == desired)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                occurrences++;</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Check for the desired number and count it</cline>
          <cline>            if (nums[i][j] != desired)</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                occurrences++;</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        } // end inner for loop</cline>
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    // Return the count of occurrences after checking every element</cline>
        <cline>    return occurrences;</cline>
        <cline>} // end numOccurrences method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex7muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex7muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional int array and return a single dimensional (normal) int
        array containing the average of each of the columns. But, the blocks
        have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not needed in
        a correct solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and put them in
        the correct order on the right. Click the Check button to check your
        solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="10">
        <cline>public static int[] averageCols(int[][] nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    // Create the result array with one place for each column</cline>
        <cline>    int[] averages = new int[nums[0].length];</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="11">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each column index of the given array</cline>
          <cline>    for (int col = 0; col &lt; nums[0].length; col++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each column index of the given array</cline>
          <cline>    for (int col = 0; col &lt; nums.length; col++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>        // Start the column's running total at zero</cline>
        <cline>        int colSum = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each row index of this column</cline>
        <cline>        for (int row = 0; row &lt; nums.length; row++)</cline>
        <cline>        {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Add the element at this row and column to the column's running total</cline>
          <cline>            colSum += nums[row][col];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Add the element at this row and column to the column's running total</cline>
          <cline>            colSum += nums[col][row];</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>        } // end inner for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Turn the column's running total into its average and store it</cline>
          <cline>        averages[col] = colSum / nums.length;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Turn the column's running total into its average and store it</cline>
          <cline>        averages[col] = colSum / nums[0].length;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Turn the column's running total into its average and store it</cline>
          <cline>        averages[col] = colSum / nums.length();</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>    // Return the array holding the column averages</cline>
        <cline>    return averages;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>} // end averageCols method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex8muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex8muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="show" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional int array and return a new two-dimensional int array
        containing only the odd index rows. But, the blocks have been mixed up
        and include extra blocks that are not needed in a correct
        solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left and put them in the
        correct order on the right. Click the Check button to check your
        solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="8">
        <cline>public static int[][] oddRows(int[][] nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    // Create the result array and a counter starting at its first row</cline>
        <cline>    int[][] odds = new int[nums.length / 2][nums[0].length];</cline>
        <cline>    int index = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the given array</cline>
        <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; nums.length; i++)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="10">
        <cline>        // Check for a row at an odd index</cline>
        <cline>        if (i % 2 == 1)</cline>
        <cline>        {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>            // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
        <cline>            for (int j = 0; j &lt; nums[i].length; j++)</cline>
        <cline>            {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>                // Copy the element into the result at the counter's row</cline>
          <cline>                odds[index][j] = nums[i][j];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>                // Copy the element into the result at the counter's row</cline>
          <cline>                odds[index][j] = nums[j][i];</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>            } // end inner for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Move the counter past the row just copied</cline>
          <cline>            index++;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Move the counter past the row just copied</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
          <cline>        index++;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
        <cline>    return odds;</cline>
        <cline>} // end oddRows method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex9muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex9muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional String array, in which each row contains the characters
        of a word. The method should return a single-dimensional (normal) String
        array containing the words in each row of the two-dimensional array.
      </p>

      <p>
        Take for example, the input 2d array: <pre>{ {“b”, “a”, “t”, “h”}, {“t”,
        “e”, “n”, “s”}, {“j”, “a”, “c”, “k”}, {“l”, “a”, “z”, “y”} } </pre>
      </p>

      <p>Resulting array: {“bath”, “tens”, “jack”, “lazy”}</p>
      <p>
        But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are
        not needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed code from the left
        to the right and put them in order with the correct indention so that
        the code would work correctly. Click the Check button to check your
        solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="10">
        <cline>public static String[] breakIntoLetters(String[][] words)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Create the result array with one place for each word</cline>
          <cline>    String[] result = new String[words.length];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Create the result array with one place for each word</cline>
          <cline>    String[] result = new String[words[0].length];</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="11">
        <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the given array</cline>
        <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; words.length; i++)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Start this row's word as an empty string</cline>
          <cline>        String word = "";</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Start this row's word as an empty string</cline>
          <cline>        String word;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each column index of this row</cline>
        <cline>        for (int j = 0; j &lt; words[i].length; j++)</cline>
        <cline>        {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Add the letter at this column to the end of the row's word</cline>
          <cline>            word += words[i][j];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Add the letter at this column to the end of the row's word</cline>
          <cline>            word = words[i][j];</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>        } // end inner for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Put the row's word into the result</cline>
        <cline>        result[i] = word;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    // Return the array holding the words</cline>
        <cline>    return result;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>} // end breakIntoLetters method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="array2Dex10muc-sgl" xml:id="array2Dex10muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should accept a
        two-dimensional int array, and return a single-dimensional (normal) int
        array containing the max of each row. But, the blocks have been mixed up
        and include extra blocks that are not needed in a correct solution.
        Drag the needed code from the left to the right and put them in order
        with the correct indention so that the code would work correctly. Click
        the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="10">
        <cline>public static int[] maxEachRow(int[][] nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Create the result array with one place for each row</cline>
          <cline>    int[] max = new int[nums.length];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Create the result array with one place for each row</cline>
          <cline>    int[] max = new int[nums[0].length];</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="11">
        <cline>    // Use an outer for loop to visit each row index of the given array</cline>
        <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; nums.length; i++)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Start with the row's first element as the largest so far</cline>
          <cline>        int maxVal = nums[i][0];</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Start with the row's first element as the largest so far</cline>
          <cline>        int maxVal = nums[0][0];</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each remaining column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int j = 1; j &lt; nums[i].length; j++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Use an inner for loop to visit each remaining column index of this row</cline>
          <cline>        for (int j = 1; j &lt; nums.length; j++)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>            // Replace the largest so far when you find a larger element</cline>
          <cline>            if (maxVal &lt; nums[i][j])</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                maxVal = nums[i][j];</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>            // Replace the largest so far when you find a larger element</cline>
          <cline>            if (maxVal &gt; nums[i][j])</cline>
          <cline>            {</cline>
          <cline>                maxVal = nums[i][j];</cline>
          <cline>            } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>        } // end inner for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>        // Put the row's largest element into the result</cline>
        <cline>        max[i] = maxVal;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    } // end outer for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>    // Return the array holding the max of each row</cline>
        <cline>    return max;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>} // end maxEachRow method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
